{"id":"leetcode-1929","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Concatenation of Array","summary":"Given an integer array nums of length n, generate an array ans of length 2n where ans[i] equals nums[i] and ans[i + n] equals nums[i] for 0 <= i < n.","statement":"Given an integer array nums of length n, generate an array ans of length 2n where ans[i] equals nums[i] and ans[i + n] equals nums[i] for 0 <= i < n. This results in ans being the combination of two nums arrays.","constraints":["nums has 1 through 1000 positive values.","Return an array of length twice len(nums).","The first and second halves must both equal nums in their original order."],"topics":["arrays","simulation"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"concatenate_array_twice","parameters":[{"name":"nums","annotation":"list[int]","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"list[int]","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def concatenate_array_twice(nums: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def concatenate_array_twice(nums):\n    return nums + nums\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def concatenate_array_twice(nums):\n    return nums\n","def concatenate_array_twice(nums):\n    return nums + list(reversed(nums))\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(n)","target_space_complexity":"O(n)","estimated_minutes":20,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":1,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":0,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["The result consists of two independent copies of the input sequence.","Use list concatenation to place one complete copy after the other.","Return the new list.","Concatenation preserves each operand's order and length, so the result satisfies both required halves and has exactly twice the input length."],"editorial":"Concatenation preserves each operand's order and length, so the result satisfies both required halves and has exactly twice the input length.","tests":[{"id":"lc-1929-1","arguments":[[1,2,1]],"expected":[1,2,1,1,2,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Placing two copies consecutively gives [1,2,1,1,2,1].","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-1929-2","arguments":[[1,3,2,1]],"expected":[1,3,2,1,1,3,2,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"The result is [1,3,2,1,1,3,2,1].","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-1929-3","arguments":[[1]],"expected":[1,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-1929-4","arguments":[[5,5]],"expected":[5,5,5,5],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-1929-5","arguments":[[1,2,3,4]],"expected":[1,2,3,4,1,2,3,4],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-1929-6","arguments":[[9,8,7]],"expected":[9,8,7,9,8,7],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-1929-7","arguments":[[10,20]],"expected":[10,20,10,20],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-1929-8","arguments":[[4,1,4,1]],"expected":[4,1,4,1,4,1,4,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-1929-9","arguments":[[1000]],"expected":[1000,1000],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-1929-10","arguments":[[2,3,5,7]],"expected":[2,3,5,7,2,3,5,7],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-1929-11","arguments":[[6,6,6]],"expected":[6,6,6,6,6,6],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-1929-12","arguments":[[1,9,2,8,3]],"expected":[1,9,2,8,3,1,9,2,8,3],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-1929-13","arguments":[[7,4,2,9]],"exp